> Personally, I'm in agreement with you. But I'm working on describing the=
=20
> unfinished cmavo entries in the BPFK sections, this is one of the=20
> entries, and that's it's official definition, stupid as it is.
>=20
> I would like to at this time seek approval for removing the following=20
> entries from the BPFK Section: Tense=20
> <http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=3DBPFK+Section%3A+Tense> =
page:
>=20
> {baba}=B9
> {bapu}=B9
> {puba}=B9
> {pupu}=B9

At the time these were added, they were the best Lojban equivalents of=20
certain aspects.  We later added another set of cmavo that solved the=20
problem in a different way, but it was not clear that the two systems=20
were totally redundant.  This was before the "Imaginary Journeys=20
paradigm" was invented.

> {baca'a}=B2
> {caca'a}=B2
> {cajeba}=B2
> {puca'a}=B2
> {pujeba}=B2
> {pujeca}=B2
> {puza}=B2
> {puze'a}=B2
> {puze'i}=B2
> {puze'u}=B2
> {puzi}=B2
> {puzu}=B2

These and many other compounds were added to the cmavo list to show how=20
cmavo could be used in combination within the grammar, and incidentally=20
to provide Lojban equivalents for certain English usages and expressions.

There was no CLL at the time, and most Lojbanists did not learn or=20
understand the grammar from the YACC or EBNF formats, but from these=20
sorts of compounds being present in the cmavo list, with translations.

> =B9 Official meaning differs from usage.

If these differ, it should be relatively easy to demonstrate this, and=20
show what they SHOULD mean.  Eliminating them is a change (to the cmavo=20
list which is a baseline document), and needs to be justified.

I suspect that I will agree with you that either they shouldn't be kept,=20
or that their meaning needs to be changed/clarified.

 >as well as being non-intuitive

One would want any non-intuitive compounds to be explicitly documented.

> =B2 Meaning is obvious given meaning of components and therefore does not=
=20
> need it's own entry.

Possible true for someone with a thorough understanding of the=20
components and how they work together.  But such understanding isn't=20
something that should be presumed of the typical user of the books and=20
wordlists.  Lots of examples are good!

Equally important, again, is that there is an English-to-Lojban=20
direction for a dictionary or word list, and not just a=20
Lojban-to-English direction. (Replace English by any other language as=20
desired.)  That we usually look at wordlists in Lojban-to-English order=20
doesn't reflect that they were designed for use in both directions.

(Given the difference in the various natural languages, different=20
natural languages would probably warrant different compounds being shown=20
in their respective bilingual lists.)

In my own half-completed definition of "pu" I was planning on including=20
those (pu) compounds that had indeed seen usage in the corpus (some of=20
which are not in the cmavo list), and then arguing for elimination of=20
the rest as not necessary for pedagogical or usage reasons.

